pe": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Speaking", "type": "skill"}]}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self-Assessment.", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 11, "stimuli_ids": []}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Sally Gets a Job at a Magazine", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Sally's First Assignment", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The First Conditional ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use the first conditional to talk about actions and situations that are possible in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "There are two parts to the sentence.<br/><br/>  One part is the <span class=\"strong\">condition</span>. The other part is the <span class=\"strong\">result</span>. <br/><br/>Form:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">If</span>* + <span class=\"italic\">subject</span> + <span class=\"italic\">Simple Present tense</span>  + <span class=\"italic\">subject</span> + <span class=\"italic\">will/won't</span><br/>You use a comma after the condition in this form.<br/><br/>  *You can use other words instead of <span class=\"italic\">if</span>. You can use <span class=\"italic\">before</span>, <span class=\"italic\">after</span> or <span class=\"italic\">when</span>. <br/><br/>  You can flip the two parts of the sentence so that the result comes first. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Before you start, </span><br/><br/>  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">After your meeting,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">you may want to speak to the editor.</span><br/><br/>   <span class=\\\"italic\\\">we will chat.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "</br>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You'll need to give me a draft of your article</span><br/><br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">This will be your first assignment</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">when you come to see me.</span><br/><br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\">if this is of interest to you.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "editor-in-chief", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the person who is in charge of a group of editors (the editorial team)", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I am your boss and editor-in-chief of this magazine.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about working at a magazine.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Asking for Clarification", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "If you don't understand what a person is saying, it is important to ask for clarification in a polite way.<br/><br/>Here are some expressions you can use to ask for clarification:", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<ul> <li><span class=\"italic\">I'm not quite sure what you mean.</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">Sorry. I didn't get that (point)?</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">What do you mean by ... ?</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">Did you say ... ?</span><l/i> <li><span class=\"italic\">Could you clarify that?</span></li> <li><span class=\"italic\">Could you give me an example?</span></li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ms. Ryan, could you please clarify what it is I will write about? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Did you say a feature on the citizens?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Sorry. I didn't get your point about the new editor. ", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "copy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "something that is made to look exactly like another thing ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Here is a copy for you to keep.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "editorial calendar", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a schedule for future issues of a magazine ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You will find this editorial calendar to be very helpful when you are planning your articles. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to focus on ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to give special attention to something ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We will focus on the the citizens of Massachusetts.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "feature", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a piece or pieces of writing about a subject in a magazine", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": " Example: We want to do a feature on important citizens. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "public figure", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person who is well-known to the public ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We want to focus on public figures. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "notable ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "important; well-known ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are many notable public figures in America. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "draft", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a piece of writing or a plan that is not finished  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You may bring me a draft of your article when you come in.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob07aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "assignment", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a piece of work that someone asks you to do", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This will be your first assignment with Cambridge Life.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob07aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to fit in", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to see someone, even when you have a lot of other things to do  ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I hope he can fit me into his busy schedule.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le16ob07aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Think of important people in your city. Write their names down.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "From your list, choose a person you would like to write about. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do some research about them. What is their name? What was their job? Why are they important? What do or did they do? When were they born?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a paragraph using the information you found. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Proofread your paragraph. Read it to a friend.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write about a public figure in my city.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about their work and job.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I tell a friend about a public figure.", "type": "text"}]}]}